          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "die Debatte — \"the debate\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Im Parlament gibt es heute eine Debatte über die Schulen. Today there is a debate in parliament about schools."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: die Debatten. More formal and more public than die Diskussion."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Debatte was borrowed from French; EtymDB links it to débattre, Old French debatre \"to fight, to contend\". That verb is built on battre \"to beat\", from Latin battuere \"to beat\" (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
