          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "betonen is built on Ton \"tone, accent\", which came through Latin tonus \"a sound, a tone\" (Lewis & Short) from Greek tónos \"a stretching, a tone\": you give a word more tone."
            }
          ]
        },
